    "title": "Nearly $1 Million in Funding Awarded to Local Communities, Reichard Says",
    "url": "https://repreichard.com/News/38696/Press-Releases/Nearly--1-Million-in-Funding-Awarded-to-Local-Communities--Reichard-Says",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Nearly $1 Million in Funding Awarded to Local Communities, Reichard Says\nSeptember 15, 2026\nWAYNESBORO –\nRep. Chad Reichard (R-Franklin) announced that several communities in the 90th Legislative District received nearly $1 million in funding through Local Share Account (LSA) grants.\n“This funding will aid communities across the district with fulfilling vital, unique needs,” Reichard said. “I’m pleased to have supported projects that will have positive impacts on the lives of residents in the district.”\nThe following municipalities were awarded grants:\n•\tMercersburg Borough,\non behalf of the\nMercersburg Water Authority,\nreceived\n$500,000\nto install 30 valves and replace 493 outdated residential meters and a master meter to improve billing accuracy and deploy automated valve exercising equipment to ensure long-term system reliability.\n•\tAntrim Township,\non behalf of\nRescue Hose Company #1 Fire Engine,\nreceived\n$250,000\nfor the purchase of a new fire engine to replace its 25-year-old apparatus.\n•\tWaynesboro Borough,\non behalf of the\nWaynesboro Area YMCA,\nreceived\n$200,000\nto renovate its two gymnasiums, including upgrades to HVAC, electrical systems, roofing, flooring, doors, paint and other infrastructure.\n•\tWaynesboro Borough\nreceived\n$25,509\nto purchase 21 new TASER devices, replacing outdated models.\n“Mercersburg’s aging water system has reached a point where these upgrades are necessary to improve reliability and address deficiencies before they become larger and more costly problems,” Reichard said. “This investment will modernize critical infrastructure, allow the authority to better manage repairs and disruptions, and help ensure Mercersburg residents have a dependable water system.”\nThe grants were approved and awarded by the Commonwealth Financing Authority, which was established as an independent agency that holds fiduciary responsibility over the funding of programs and investments in Pennsylvania’s economic growth. LSA grants are derived from gaming revenues.\nRepresentative Chad Reichard\n90th Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Greg Gross\n717.260.6374\nggross@pahousegop.com\nRepReichard.com\n/\nFacebook.com/RepReichard\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "The Commonwealth Financing Authority approved Local Share Account grants totaling approximately $975,509 for four projects in Pennsylvania's 90th Legislative District. The grants will fund water system upgrades in Mercersburg, a new fire engine for Antrim Township, YMCA gymnasium renovations in Waynesboro, and new TASER devices for Waynesboro Borough. Rep. Reichard announced the grants but did not author the grant program; LSA funds are derived from gaming revenues and distributed by an independent state agency.",
      "action_type": "statement",
      "topics": [
        "infrastructure",
