    "raw_text": "Reichard Bill to Protect Children, Strengthen Police Response to Indecent Exposure\nSeptember 1, 2026\nWAYNESBORO – Sparked by a reported indecent exposure incident in a Washington Township park, Rep. Chad Reichard (R-Franklin) will soon introduce legislation granting police the power to make an on-scene arrest during such cases.\nUnder current Pennsylvania law, police must witness indecent exposures firsthand to make an on-scene arrest without a warrant.\n“I was astonished to learn from police that an on-scene arrest couldn’t be made when a man was seen by others exposing himself near a park where children play,” Reichard said. “I quickly got to work to right this wrong and a bill to fix this issue will soon be introduced.”\nAccording to Washington Township Police, officers responded to Red Run Park for a reported indecent exposure incident. Though police gathered enough information indicating an alleged crime took place near the playground area, and officers deemed the offense met the level of a misdemeanor, officers could not make an on-scene arrest since they did not personally witness the act. Charges have since been filed.\nReichard’s forthcoming legislation would establish an exception for indecent exposure, allowing an officer to make an on-scene arrest when the officer has probable cause to believe the offense has been committed.\nState law already provides for warrantless arrests for certain misdemeanors, including offenses such as scattering rubbish. This legislation would similarly give police the authority to respond promptly and appropriately to allegations of indecent exposure.\n“Parents should be able to take their children to a local park without worrying that someone who exposes themselves can simply walk away because an officer didn’t happen to witness the act,” Reichard said. “Our police officers need the tools and authority to protect our communities. This legislation will help ensure they can take action when there is probable cause that an indecent exposure has occurred.”\nRepresentative Chad Reichard\n90th Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Greg Gross\n717.260.6374\nggross@pahousegop.com\nRepReichard.com / Facebook.com/RepReichard\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Rep. Chad Reichard announced plans to introduce a bill that would allow police to make warrantless on-scene arrests for indecent exposure when they have probable cause, even if they did not personally witness the act. Current Pennsylvania law requires officers to witness the offense directly to arrest without a warrant. The bill has not yet been introduced.",
      "action_type": "bill_introduced",
      "topics": [
        "public_safety"
