    "title": "Reichard Secures More Than $775,000 for Safer Schools",
    "url": "https://repreichard.com/News/38496/Press-Releases/Reichard-Secures-More-Than--775-000-for-Safer-Schools",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Reichard Secures More Than $775,000 for Safer Schools\nAugust 14, 2026\nWAYNESBORO\n– Schools in the 90th Legislative District received $775,429 in funding from the Pennsylvania Commission on Crime and Delinquency’s (PCCD) School Safety and Security Committee (SSC) to improve safety for students, Rep. Chad Reichard (R-Franklin) announced.\n“I’m pleased to see our districts being proactive in promoting safety for children who attend our schools,” Reichard said. “This funding will assist districts with improving security for students so that they can learn in safe environments.”\nSchool districts in the 90th Legislative District to receive grants are:\n•\nFranklin County Career and Technology Center: $70,000.\n•\nGreencastle-Antrim School District: $224,239.\n•\nTuscarora School District: $196,110.\n•\nWaynesboro Area School District: $285,080.\nThe PCCD’s School Safety and Security Committee awards grants to schools and organizations across Pennsylvania to improve safety measures and provide essential mental health services for students and staff.\nRepresentative Chad Reichard\n90th Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Greg Gross\n717.260.6374\nggross@pahousegop.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Four school districts in Pennsylvania's 90th Legislative District received a combined $775,429 in state grants through the Pennsylvania Commission on Crime and Delinquency's School Safety and Security Committee. The funds are designated for improving school security measures and mental health services. Rep. Reichard announced the grants but did not author the grant program.",
      "action_type": "statement",
      "topics": [
        "education",
        "public_safety"
      ],
      "spin_flag": true
    }
  },
